   "name": "Drug abuse: cigarette smoking"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Cigarette smoke contains thousands of chemicals, including:\n• nicotine: makes smokers addicted and raises the heart rate and blood pressure;\n• tar: sticky, coats the lungs and causes cancer;\n• carbon monoxide: takes the place of oxygen in the blood.\nHealth effects: lung cancer and cancers of the mouth and throat, bronchitis and coughing, emphysema (damaged air sacs), heart disease, stained teeth, bad breath, less fitness. Babies of smoking mothers are often small.\nPassive smoking: people near a smoker breathe in the smoke and are harmed too.\nSocial effects: money wasted, bad smell, fires, setting a bad example.\nSmoking in public places is forbidden in Cameroon, and the sale of tobacco to minors is forbidden. Shisha (water pipe) is also harmful.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "c": "carbon monoxide"
  },
  "problem": "How does {c} in cigarette smoke harm the body?",
  "steps": [
   "It joins the red blood cells in place of oxygen.",
   "Less oxygen reaches the body, so the smoker is short of breath and the heart works harder."
  ],
  "answer": "It reduces the oxygen carried by the blood.",
  "checks": []
 },
